    "error_map":  {},
    "_error_map_note":  "GitHub REST API is pure HTTP -- no numeric provider error codes. Error bodies use {\"message\": \"Bad credentials\"} format; classify_http_error extracts provider codes from 'error.code', 'error_code', or 'code' fields only, so no error_map keys will ever fire for GitHub (the body carries no extractable code). Pure-HTTP classification applies: 401 -> auth_expired, 403 -> permission_denied. The 403 rate-limit case is architecturally ambiguous: GitHub sends 403 (not 429) with X-RateLimit-Remaining:0 headers when the primary rate limit is exceeded; secondary rate limits may return 429. The connector currently raises a raw PermissionError on all 403s (pre-25.2 code path in _pull_releases/_pull_deployments) rather than routing through classify_http_error. Splitting 403 rate-limit vs 403 permission-denied requires header inspection, which classify_http_error does not support. Deferred to a future connector refactor (post-25.7). 429 handling per core.quota.RateLimitError contract is a no-op in practice until the connector migrates off raw PermissionError.",
    "_account_topology_note":  "Token-scoped context source: one PAT or OAuth token addresses exactly one repository (owner+repo stored in Nango connection metadata). No account discovery hierarchy exists -- the repository itself is the root scope. account_topology is not declared.",
